      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nMetformin 4250 mg three times daily comes to **12,750 mg/day**. The FDA-labeled maximum for adults is **2,550 mg/day**, usually given as 850 mg three times daily. This order is 5 times that. A dose this high carries a serious risk of metformin-associated lactic acidosis, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **425 mg** three times daily (a decimal or extra-digit error)\n- **850 mg** three times daily (the standard maximum of 2,550 mg/day)\n- **500 mg or 1000 mg** with meals, depending on the titration plan\n\nIf 4250 mg per dose is what you intend, for example in a protocol I'm not aware of, tell me and I'll enter it with a note recording that you confirmed the dose. Otherwise, give me the corrected dose and I'll enter it right away."
      }
